  - m_Id: 22644383744
    m_Localized: BAKU - Police have discovered multiple deceased individuals at an
      abandoned industrial facility outside Baku, according to sources within the
      Ministry of Interior. The discovery was made early Tuesday morning following
      an anonymous tip received by authorities. Minister of Interior Ramil Usubov
      confirmed the discovery during a brief press conference but declined to provide
      specific details about the number of victims or circumstances surrounding their
      deaths.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22644383745
    m_Localized: Multiple Bodies Discovered at Industrial Site
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22644383746
    m_Localized: 'By Leyla Mammadova, Crime Reporter | Published: March 15, 2003,
      08:30 AM | Updated: March 15, 2003, 11:45 AM'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22648578048
    m_Localized: "BAKU - Police have discovered multiple deceased individuals at
      an abandoned industrial facility outside Baku, according to sources within
      the Ministry of Interior. The discovery was made early Tuesday morning following
      an anonymous tip received by authorities.\n\nMinister of Interior Ramil Usubov
      confirmed the discovery during a brief press conference but declined to provide
      specific details about the number of victims or circumstances surrounding their
      deaths.\n\n\"Investigation is ongoing and details are being withheld to protect
      case integrity,\" Usubov stated. \"We ask the public to report any suspicious
      activities to authorities and emphasize that public safety is not at risk.\"\n\nThe
      facility, identified as the former Ny\xC9\u2122m Film Processing Plant, was
      abandoned in the late 1990s following the collapse of several state-owned industrial
      operations. Local residents reported increased police presence in the area
      since Tuesday morning.\n\nA special task force has been formed to investigate
      the incident, according to police sources who spoke on condition of anonymity.
      The investigation is being led by the Criminal Investigation Department with
      assistance from forensic specialists.\n\nNo connection has been established
      to other criminal cases at this time, officials emphasized. The abandoned facility
      had been scheduled for demolition as part of urban redevelopment plans.\n\nThis
      is a developing story. The Baku Daily Chronicle will continue to provide updates
      as more information becomes available."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
